<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Untitled Document</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 40px 30px;
            line-height: 1.4;
            color: black;
        }
        .header {
            font-size: 24px;
            font-weight: bold;
            text-align: center;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            border-bottom: 1px solid black;
            padding-bottom: 10px;
        }
        .section {
            margin-bottom: 30px;
        }
        .section-title {
            font-size: 16px;
            font-weight: bold;
            margin-bottom: 8px;
            text-decoration: underline;
        }
        ul {
            margin-left: 20px;
            padding-left: 10px;
        }
        li {
            margin-bottom: 6px;
        }
        .placeholder {
            width: 100%;
            height: 80px;
            border: 1px dashed #999;
            background-color: #f0f0f0;
            margin: 15px 0;
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            font-style: italic;
            color: #666;
            text-align: center;
            font-size: 14px;
        }
        table {
            width: 100%;
            border-collapse: collapse;
            margin: 15px 0;
        }
        th, td {
            border: 1px solid black;
            padding: 8px;
            text-align: left;
        }
        th {
            background-color: #e0e0e0;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="header">
    Sample Document Layout
</div>

<div class="section">
    <div class="section-title">Title</div>
    <p><strong>This is a sample document</strong> to demonstrate OCR-to-HTML conversion with exact layout fidelity.</p>
</div>

<div class="section">
    <div class="section-title">Body Text</div>
    <p>This is the first paragraph. It continues with more text that may wrap to the next line depending on the font and window size.</p>
    <p>Second paragraph follows immediately. Short sentences are used to show spacing.</p>
</div>

<div class="section">
    <div class="section-title">Lists</div>
    <ol>
        <li>First item in ordered list</li>
        <li>Second item in ordered list</li>
        <li>Third item in ordered list</li>
    </ol>
    <ul>
        <li>Bullet point one</li>
        <li>Bullet point two</li>
        <li>Bullet point three</li>
    </ul>
</div>

<div class="section">
    <div class="section-title">Table Example</div>
    <table>
        <tr>
            <th>Header 1</th>
            <th>Header 2</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>Cell 1</td>
            <td>Cell 2</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>Cell 3</td>
            <td>Cell 4</td>
        </tr>
    </table>
</div>

<div class="section">
    <div class="section-title">Horizontal Line</div>
    <hr style="border: 1px solid black; margin: 15px 0;">
</div>

<div class="section">
    <div class="section-title">Image Placeholder (exactly where it appears)</div>
    <div class="placeholder">
        [Image: top-center, 300px wide]
    </div>
</div>

<div class="section">
    <div class="section-title">Poetic / Address Block</div>
    <p style="text-align: center; font-style: italic;">
        This is a centered block with<br>
        multiple lines of text.<br>
        It demonstrates block-level positioning.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="section">
    <div class="section-title">Footer Text</div>
    <p style="text-align: center; font-size: 12px; color: gray;">
        This document was generated as a faithful recreation of the original spatial layout.
    </p>
</div>

</body>
</html>
